1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:06,080
Characters, actions, places, occupations,
and events in this series

2
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:08,750
are fictional and created
for entertainment purposes only.

3
00:00:08,790 --> 00:00:13,290
They are not intended to urge
or promote any behavior in the series.

4
00:00:13,320 --> 00:00:15,730
Viewer discretion is advised.

5
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,100
I’m Key.

6
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:18,610
This is my first day working here.

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,640
I met someone.

8
00:00:21,850 --> 00:00:24,300
So this one night, it must be really good.

9
00:00:24,470 --> 00:00:26,370
You don’t seem to have a money problem.

10
00:00:26,410 --> 00:00:28,100
Why do you want to be my sugar baby?

11
00:00:28,380 --> 00:00:29,980
I just want to be your girl.

12
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:32,400
I chose to get the moon tattoo
because of you.

13
00:00:32,640 --> 00:00:34,160
You are my first love.

14
00:00:34,830 --> 00:00:36,080
Have we met before?

15
00:00:36,490 --> 00:00:37,690
I won’t tell you if we have met.

16
00:00:38,030 --> 00:00:39,900
You have to remember it yourself.

17
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,350
Mom.

18
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:47,980
Mom.

19
00:00:50,670 --> 00:00:51,950
-Mom.
-Miss.

20
00:00:58,090 --> 00:01:00,270
-Mom.
-Key.

21
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:06,630
Mom

22
00:01:06,680 --> 00:01:08,200
What happened to my wife?

23
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,289
There’s not much I can tell you right now.

24
00:01:10,680 --> 00:01:14,900
We need to wait for the autopsy results
to know her cause of death.

25
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:19,600
I need your daughter to come
to the station to give her statement.

26
00:01:20,380 --> 00:01:21,200
Why?

27
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:24,300
Because she is the first person
who discovered the body.

28
00:01:26,630 --> 00:01:28,780
This is my fault, Dad.

29
00:01:32,090 --> 00:01:34,700
She is dead because I came back home.

30
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:36,800
Key, don’t say anything.

31
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,580
It’s my fault that she is dead.

32
00:01:39,620 --> 00:01:40,479
Key.

33
00:01:40,509 --> 00:01:42,060
It’s my fault that she is dead.

34
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:45,580
Honey, don’t say that.

35
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:53,170
It’s my fault that she is dead.

36
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:55,800
It’s not your fault.

37
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:57,800
It’s my fault.

38
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:01,400
Key, don’t do this.

39
00:02:03,400 --> 00:02:04,210
Key.

40
00:02:08,970 --> 00:02:11,100
It’s my fault that she is dead.

41
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:13,500
It’s not your fault.

42
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:18,329
I shouldn’t have come back.

43
00:02:18,700 --> 00:02:19,450
Key.

44
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:21,200
I shouldn’t have come back.

45
00:03:30,620 --> 00:03:32,300
Tonight is a new moon night.

46
00:03:34,070 --> 00:03:34,780
Is that so?

47
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:36,900
So what?

48
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:46,170
They say a new moon, or a moonless night,

49
00:03:48,210 --> 00:03:50,380
it marks a new beginning.

50
00:03:52,100 --> 00:03:53,850
It’s a chance to wash away the negative

51
00:03:55,130 --> 00:03:57,000
and transform into
a new version of ourselves.

52
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,380
It’s a good time

53
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:07,180
for those who want to forget
the bad things in their past

54
00:04:08,990 --> 00:04:10,780
or for those who have done bad things.

55
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:15,200
Tonight is a good chance.

56
00:04:16,750 --> 00:04:18,120
Is something going on with you?

57
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:20,890
Yes.

58
00:04:22,720 --> 00:04:23,980
Something big is going on.

59
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:26,330
What is it?

60
00:04:27,830 --> 00:04:29,630
I want to be your sugar baby.

61
00:04:31,960 --> 00:04:34,070
Why do you keep saying the same thing?

62
00:04:35,530 --> 00:04:37,670
This is the last time I’ll ask you.

63
00:04:39,240 --> 00:04:41,100
If you don’t want me to talk about it,

64
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,290
then you need to give me your answer.

65
00:04:44,450 --> 00:04:47,900
What are you going to do about us?

66
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:53,930
Why do you want to be my sugar baby?

67
00:04:54,690 --> 00:04:56,000
It will be fun.

68
00:04:57,350 --> 00:05:01,710
I like being your little sugar baby.

69
00:05:02,480 --> 00:05:03,890
You are strange.

70
00:05:05,030 --> 00:05:06,250
If I’m not strange,

71
00:05:07,010 --> 00:05:08,570
you won’t remember me.

72
00:05:11,230 --> 00:05:13,400
Do you have anything else
for me to remember,

73
00:05:14,540 --> 00:05:16,000
besides your strange offer?

74
00:05:18,550 --> 00:05:20,400
Something else to remember?

75
00:05:21,640 --> 00:05:22,900
What else could it be?

76
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:25,500
Pretty sis.

77
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:32,380
If you want to be my sugar baby,

78
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:34,200
you need to follow my rules.

79
00:05:35,690 --> 00:05:36,480
Rules?

80
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:43,130
I can do anything to you.

81
00:05:44,100 --> 00:05:48,570
But you need to do everything I tell you.

82
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,200
You are mine only.

83
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:56,380
But it doesn’t mean

84
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:59,600
that I will have only you.

85
00:06:02,940 --> 00:06:04,780
Then what am I to you?

86
00:06:06,380 --> 00:06:07,500
My sugar baby.

87
00:06:08,260 --> 00:06:09,840
I own you.

88
00:06:10,790 --> 00:06:11,900
I’m your boss.

89
00:06:13,810 --> 00:06:14,900
Are you okay with it?

90
00:06:15,490 --> 00:06:16,700
If not,

91
00:06:17,320 --> 00:06:18,410
then we will go our separate ways.

92
00:06:31,090 --> 00:06:32,020
Okay.

93
00:06:33,430 --> 00:06:34,900
I’ll be your sugar baby.

94
00:06:37,300 --> 00:06:38,810
Are you sure you are okay with it?

95
00:06:40,330 --> 00:06:43,600
A woman like you is so my type.

96
00:06:44,740 --> 00:06:45,600
I like you.

97
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:51,800
I’ll remind you again.

98
00:06:52,570 --> 00:06:56,000
Between us, I’m your employer.

99
00:06:56,780 --> 00:06:59,100
You are my employee.

100
00:07:00,840 --> 00:07:02,300
And…

101
00:07:04,390 --> 00:07:06,800
You are my personal entertainer.

102
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:13,170
No one can know about our deal.

103
00:07:14,320 --> 00:07:15,300
Roger that.

104
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:21,050
Are you going to spend tonight with me?

105
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:24,330
So I can start providing my service.

106
00:08:07,530 --> 00:08:08,400
Key.

107
00:08:10,500 --> 00:08:11,430
What’s wrong?

108
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,080
Why are you sleeping here?

109
00:08:18,500 --> 00:08:21,700
Simba kept waking me.

110
00:08:23,870 --> 00:08:25,800
So I came out to give him wet cat food.

111
00:08:25,850 --> 00:08:27,120
But he refused to eat it.

112
00:08:28,630 --> 00:08:30,080
So I boiled chicken for him.

113
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:32,250
He also refused to eat it.

114
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:39,200
Let me take a look.

115
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:45,950
Key.

116
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,650
Get up. Go get dressed.

117
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:50,700
Where are we going?

118
00:08:50,910 --> 00:08:52,480
We’ll take Simba to see a vet.

119
00:08:53,300 --> 00:08:55,550
We don’t need to. This is typical of him.

120
00:08:55,590 --> 00:08:56,690
He’s just a free spirit.

121
00:08:58,200 --> 00:09:00,400
If you refuse to eat,

122
00:09:00,780 --> 00:09:02,730
is it because you’re sick,
or you’re just a free spirit?

123
00:09:05,450 --> 00:09:06,400
Sick.

124
00:09:08,980 --> 00:09:11,400
Don’t worry. I’ll take you to a vet.

125
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,900
Let’s take him to a vet.

126
00:09:28,240 --> 00:09:29,800
It’s okay, Simba.

127
00:09:30,590 --> 00:09:31,970
I’ll take you to a vet.

128
00:09:35,390 --> 00:09:37,670
If I hadn’t insisted on
taking Simba to a vet,

129
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:40,250
we wouldn’t have known he was sick.

130
00:09:42,200 --> 00:09:44,500
You need to take better care of him.

131
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:47,300
What would you do
if his sickness was serious?

132
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,600
Alright.

133
00:09:50,020 --> 00:09:51,200
I was wrong.

134
00:09:55,350 --> 00:09:59,200
I’ll take Simba to live with me
until he gets better.

135
00:10:00,410 --> 00:10:01,180
Huh?

136
00:10:01,950 --> 00:10:03,100
Are you serious?

137
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:03,900
Yes.

138
00:10:04,210 --> 00:10:07,000
If you leave him alone to go to work

139
00:10:07,520 --> 00:10:09,580
and there’s an emergency,
what will you do?

140
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:13,950
I won’t let anything happen to him.

141
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,810
Simba’s mom, please go get his medication.

142
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,000
Yes.

143
00:10:29,730 --> 00:10:31,500
We are both his moms.

144
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,970
I’m his mommy.

145
00:10:36,870 --> 00:10:38,200
She is…

146
00:10:40,090 --> 00:10:41,100
his mama.

147
00:10:42,030 --> 00:10:45,400
Mama and Mommy,
please go get his medication.

148
00:10:45,840 --> 00:10:46,700
Yes.

149
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,460
Let’s go.

150
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,030
Can you get my bag for me?

151
00:10:53,630 --> 00:10:55,850
Wait for me, Mama.

152
00:11:09,970 --> 00:11:10,750
Hi, Jay.

153
00:11:11,660 --> 00:11:12,490
Do you want a coffee?

154
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:13,400
No.

155
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:22,100
Did Chan know
that I’m your business partner?

156
00:11:24,960 --> 00:11:27,900
Are you sure you want to do this?

157
00:11:29,780 --> 00:11:32,080
You need to help me get Chan back.

158
00:11:33,670 --> 00:11:36,300
Otherwise, I won’t help you
with the debt you owe me.

159
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:38,530
I think…

160
00:11:38,570 --> 00:11:42,000
If you don’t want it to become public,
you’d better make your move to help me.

161
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:00,800
Take off your shoes here.

162
00:12:01,900 --> 00:12:02,700
Okay.

163
00:12:13,330 --> 00:12:14,500
Put on the slippers.

164
00:12:20,240 --> 00:12:22,000
We are home, Simba.

165
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,220
Do you like it?

166
00:12:35,730 --> 00:12:38,900
Do you like a big room like this?

167
00:12:40,230 --> 00:12:42,900
You can put Simba’s stuff in that room.

168
00:12:43,720 --> 00:12:44,700
Yes.

169
00:12:54,050 --> 00:12:55,300
I’ll put you down.

170
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:57,300
Do you like my room?

171
00:12:57,630 --> 00:12:58,900
It’s big, right?

172
00:12:59,980 --> 00:13:00,900
You like it?

173
00:13:01,910 --> 00:13:03,410
Your meow means you like it, doesn’t it?

174
00:13:04,370 --> 00:13:05,600
You enjoy this, don’t you?

175
00:13:10,320 --> 00:13:13,730
Why do you never look at me
the way you look at Simba?

176
00:13:14,770 --> 00:13:16,100
Are you a cat?

177
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,500
But I’m the cat’s mommy.

178
00:13:19,350 --> 00:13:20,300
Meow.

179
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,770
Simba, do you want to come out?

180
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,800
Let’s go enjoy the view.

181
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:29,830
Do you like it?

182
00:13:32,850 --> 00:13:33,740
Chan.

183
00:13:35,570 --> 00:13:37,600
Can I take a nap?

184
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:40,380
I don’t want to fall asleep
on stage tonight.

185
00:13:41,030 --> 00:13:41,800
Sure.

186
00:13:43,540 --> 00:13:44,700
You are so kind.

187
00:13:50,110 --> 00:13:50,900
Hold on.

188
00:13:52,070 --> 00:13:52,690
Yes?

189
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:53,810
Where are you going?

190
00:13:55,070 --> 00:13:56,000
I’m going to take a nap.

191
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:57,730
You can take a nap

192
00:13:58,980 --> 00:13:59,890
on the sofa.

193
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,100
That’s my bed.

194
00:14:07,110 --> 00:14:08,120
Fine.

195
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:30,560
I’ll lie down properly.

196
00:14:58,430 --> 00:14:59,320
Thank you.

197
00:15:00,950 --> 00:15:02,380
How are you doing?

198
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:04,500
I feel much better.

199
00:15:14,470 --> 00:15:17,230
You want to talk to me
about my birthday party, right?

200
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:20,000
Yes.

201
00:15:20,530 --> 00:15:23,980
I want you to invite Key to your party.

202
00:15:30,840 --> 00:15:31,900
I don’t think I can.

203
00:15:34,410 --> 00:15:38,100
I think we should give it another try.

204
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,700
I mean, I can’t do that

205
00:15:41,480 --> 00:15:44,850
because I won’t hold
a birthday party this year.

206
00:15:49,030 --> 00:15:49,900
I…

207
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:54,000
I’m really busy with the farm business.

208
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:56,730
I have many things to handle.

209
00:15:57,870 --> 00:16:00,500
I think I’ll need to stay there
for several days.

210
00:16:00,930 --> 00:16:02,800
But this is your birthday.

211
00:16:03,510 --> 00:16:08,200
Just seeing you healthy again
is the best gift for me.

212
00:16:09,580 --> 00:16:14,410
But I want all of us
to be together this year.

213
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:16,000
Please.

214
00:16:17,360 --> 00:16:20,600
It’s up to Key.

215
00:16:22,310 --> 00:16:23,300
I…

216
00:16:24,980 --> 00:16:26,290
I don’t want to force her.

217
00:17:27,050 --> 00:17:27,869
Hey.

218
00:17:28,790 --> 00:17:29,900
What are you doing?

219
00:17:32,140 --> 00:17:33,520
Did you pretend to be sleeping?

220
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:35,900
No.

221
00:17:37,910 --> 00:17:39,240
I was sleeping.

222
00:17:41,530 --> 00:17:43,850
But you smell so good.

223
00:17:45,380 --> 00:17:47,800
When you come close to me,
your scent wakes me up.

224
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:49,900
You little perv.

225
00:17:50,960 --> 00:17:52,450
You are doing it first.

226
00:17:53,490 --> 00:17:54,700
What do you mean?

227
00:17:55,070 --> 00:17:56,570
I haven’t done anything.

228
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:00,800
I’m just checking if you are breathing.

229
00:18:04,320 --> 00:18:05,640
So you’re worried about me.

230
00:18:06,130 --> 00:18:07,200
So sweet of you.

231
00:18:10,440 --> 00:18:11,400
But are you sure

232
00:18:12,460 --> 00:18:15,600
you’re just checking my breathing?

233
00:18:18,470 --> 00:18:21,100
Don’t you want to check everything
like you did last night?

234
00:18:25,650 --> 00:18:27,000
You should go home.

235
00:18:29,010 --> 00:18:31,180
But it’s not time for my work.

236
00:18:32,820 --> 00:18:34,600
I still have several hours left.

237
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:36,600
Where am I going to hang out?

238
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:41,700
That’s your business, not mine.

239
00:18:43,430 --> 00:18:44,380
But…

240
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:45,500
Go.

241
00:18:53,450 --> 00:18:56,800
Okay, I’ll leave.

242
00:18:57,720 --> 00:19:00,700
I’ll go to practice with my band.

243
00:19:12,960 --> 00:19:15,030
It doesn’t matter
if you act cold towards me

244
00:19:17,090 --> 00:19:18,800
or always have to get your own way,

245
00:19:22,140 --> 00:19:26,380
as long as I can be by your side
and see your smile,

246
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:29,640
that’s enough for me.

247
00:19:57,150 --> 00:19:57,900
Go.

248
00:20:16,300 --> 00:20:17,400
Fine, I’m leaving.

249
00:20:29,410 --> 00:20:30,600
Sis.

250
00:20:37,890 --> 00:20:39,100
Who are you?

251
00:20:41,400 --> 00:20:42,600
What’s your name?

252
00:20:45,810 --> 00:20:47,050
Whose cat is it?

253
00:20:47,510 --> 00:20:48,700
What’s your name?

254
00:20:50,380 --> 00:20:51,500
Can I hold you?

255
00:20:51,750 --> 00:20:53,100
Can I hold you?

256
00:20:53,280 --> 00:20:54,300
Come on.

257
00:20:57,920 --> 00:20:59,490
You are so chubby.

258
00:21:01,850 --> 00:21:02,940
Let me take a look at you.

259
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:05,200
What’s your name?

260
00:21:05,710 --> 00:21:06,520
What’s your name?

261
00:21:06,670 --> 00:21:07,900
Why are you here?

262
00:21:10,790 --> 00:21:13,250
When did you have a cat?

263
00:21:15,140 --> 00:21:16,400
He’s not my cat.

264
00:21:17,190 --> 00:21:18,640
I take care of him for his owner.

265
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:20,880
Who is the owner?

266
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,700
You wouldn’t know her even if I told you.

267
00:21:26,710 --> 00:21:27,900
This is not good.

268
00:21:28,510 --> 00:21:31,180
There’s no way you would
take care of a cat for someone,

269
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:33,580
especially someone I don’t know.

270
00:21:34,780 --> 00:21:36,500
What happened to you?

271
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:39,900
You are overstating.

272
00:21:40,340 --> 00:21:41,370
No, I’m not.

273
00:21:41,770 --> 00:21:43,500
I’m your twin sister.

274
00:21:43,630 --> 00:21:44,600
I know you well.

275
00:21:45,550 --> 00:21:47,100
She just asked me to take care of him.

276
00:21:47,450 --> 00:21:48,600
He’s sick.

277
00:21:50,580 --> 00:21:52,500
You are sick?

278
00:21:53,110 --> 00:21:55,710
That’s why you look lethargic.

279
00:22:01,350 --> 00:22:04,600
I didn’t know that you liked animals.

280
00:22:07,130 --> 00:22:08,380
Me too.

281
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,500
I never thought that I would like cats.

282
00:22:12,990 --> 00:22:18,300
Tell me who his owner is
and what she does for a living.

283
00:22:21,800 --> 00:22:23,640
You wouldn’t know her even if I told you.

284
00:22:24,430 --> 00:22:30,730
Does this mean you got over Jay?

285
00:22:37,190 --> 00:22:39,530
Why did you come to see me today?

286
00:22:40,490 --> 00:22:42,010
If you don’t have any business with me,

287
00:22:42,210 --> 00:22:43,400
you should leave, Sun.

288
00:22:43,960 --> 00:22:45,200
Today is my day off.

289
00:22:45,470 --> 00:22:46,490
I want to spend time alone.

290
00:22:46,640 --> 00:22:50,040
Based on your answer,
I guess you are not over her.

291
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:56,700
Fine, I’ll leave.

292
00:22:57,800 --> 00:23:02,200
I know that my words upset you.

293
00:23:03,180 --> 00:23:06,660
But seriously,
when are you going to get over her?

294
00:23:54,250 --> 00:23:55,330
We meet again.

295
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:58,600
Don’t tell me that you’re also
a regular customer at this bar?

296
00:24:00,600 --> 00:24:01,600
You’re almost right.

297
00:24:02,690 --> 00:24:04,150
I’m a regular singer here.

298
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:05,610
I started to work here recently.

299
00:24:06,020 --> 00:24:06,900
Really?

300
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:08,800
Yes.

301
00:24:09,320 --> 00:24:12,300
I told you we would
run into each other often.

302
00:24:13,280 --> 00:24:14,450
Do you think it’s destiny?

303
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,400
Maybe.

304
00:24:20,820 --> 00:24:22,400
But our destiny is to be friends.

305
00:24:24,180 --> 00:24:27,200
I guess your relationship
with that person,

306
00:24:28,140 --> 00:24:29,570
it’s no longer just a one-night stand.

307
00:24:47,350 --> 00:24:48,570
Can I ask you something?

308
00:24:49,180 --> 00:24:50,050
Sure.

309
00:24:51,230 --> 00:24:55,300
If you’re dating that person for a year,

310
00:24:56,500 --> 00:24:57,900
will you still feel excited

311
00:24:59,230 --> 00:25:00,500
when kissing her?

312
00:25:06,350 --> 00:25:07,400
I think so.

313
00:25:08,140 --> 00:25:09,090
Why?

314
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:17,500
Remember my words.

315
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,850
Kissing a person you like,

316
00:25:22,260 --> 00:25:23,500
it’s like smoking.

317
00:25:25,340 --> 00:25:27,330
You only feel excited
when it’s the first kiss.

318
00:25:31,500 --> 00:25:32,560
What do you mean?

319
00:25:37,680 --> 00:25:38,700
After a while,

320
00:25:40,420 --> 00:25:41,970
it will become a habit,

321
00:25:43,980 --> 00:25:45,330
and you'll get addicted to it.

322
00:25:50,770 --> 00:25:52,300
Even when you want to quit,

323
00:25:56,330 --> 00:25:57,400
you can’t.

324
00:26:01,740 --> 00:26:03,760
What if I always feel
excited when doing it?

325
00:26:04,990 --> 00:26:06,500
It means you are lucky.

326
00:26:07,930 --> 00:26:09,200
You’ve found the one.

327
00:26:12,340 --> 00:26:15,700
So don’t make a mistake.

328
00:26:16,180 --> 00:26:17,500
Don’t let her go.

329
00:26:22,430 --> 00:26:23,900
Key, there you are.

330
00:26:24,260 --> 00:26:25,780
It’s almost time for our band to perform.

331
00:26:25,820 --> 00:26:27,090
Okay, I’ll be right there.

332
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:30,600
You can go watch my band.

333
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:32,380
See you.

334
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:04,520
You like it?

335
00:27:04,560 --> 00:27:05,700
Do you like this toy?

336
00:27:08,810 --> 00:27:09,360
Catch it.

337
00:27:09,400 --> 00:27:11,170
One, two, three, jump.

338
00:27:11,750 --> 00:27:12,900
Let me take pictures of you.

339
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:15,400
Simba, look at the camera.

340
00:27:16,170 --> 00:27:18,200
One, two, three.

341
00:27:22,860 --> 00:27:23,800
Simba.

342
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:27,100
Let’s take a selfie.

343
00:27:28,430 --> 00:27:29,980
Wow, you look at the camera.

344
00:27:40,640 --> 00:27:41,550
Wait here.

345
00:27:49,390 --> 00:27:51,500
Look, who is here to see you?

346
00:27:58,620 --> 00:28:00,840
It seems that
Simba is getting much better now.

347
00:28:01,220 --> 00:28:02,700
I’ll take him home.

348
00:28:02,890 --> 00:28:04,300
I don’t want to bother you any longer.

349
00:28:09,630 --> 00:28:11,500
You should leave.

350
00:28:12,970 --> 00:28:15,800
I’ll keep him with me tonight

351
00:28:16,890 --> 00:28:17,800
to monitor his condition.

352
00:28:19,190 --> 00:28:20,380
How can you do that?

353
00:28:20,910 --> 00:28:22,600
He’s my cat.

354
00:28:24,440 --> 00:28:27,100
I think I can take care of him
better than you.

355
00:28:32,540 --> 00:28:34,780
How about this?

356
00:28:37,730 --> 00:28:39,400
I’ll sleep over here tonight.

357
00:28:40,300 --> 00:28:41,700
I’ll help you take care of him.

358
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,180
I’ll go home tomorrow.

359
00:28:44,640 --> 00:28:46,780
Are you using this
as an excuse to stay the night?

360
00:28:46,940 --> 00:28:48,900
You did sleep over at my place.

361
00:28:49,590 --> 00:28:51,500
Why can’t I sleep over here?

362
00:28:54,850 --> 00:28:55,700
Fine.

363
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:58,200
But you will sleep on the sofa.

364
00:29:01,800 --> 00:29:03,800
Can I sleep with you in bed?

365
00:29:06,760 --> 00:29:08,400
You’re just a sugar baby.

366
00:29:09,840 --> 00:29:12,300
You can sleep in my bed
only on special occasions.

367
00:29:21,130 --> 00:29:23,160
Then I’ll make tonight a special occasion.

368
00:29:40,080 --> 00:29:41,700
Someone told me this.

369
00:29:44,420 --> 00:29:46,300
Kissing is like smoking.

370
00:29:50,150 --> 00:29:52,200
We get excited only the first time.

371
00:30:00,910 --> 00:30:02,000
Come on, Simba.

372
00:30:02,570 --> 00:30:03,600
Let’s go to bed.

373
00:30:04,560 --> 00:30:05,600
Where did he go?

374
00:30:05,920 --> 00:30:06,800
Simba.

375
00:30:16,180 --> 00:30:17,600
Why do you say things so similarly?

376
00:30:22,830 --> 00:30:23,900
Let’s go to bed.

377
00:30:28,990 --> 00:30:29,900
Good night.

378
00:31:04,910 --> 00:31:06,350
It’s been a while, Sun.

379
00:31:08,140 --> 00:31:09,580
It’s good to see you.

380
00:31:11,910 --> 00:31:13,500
You can drop your act, Jay.

381
00:31:14,560 --> 00:31:16,010
I know you hate me.

382
00:31:16,420 --> 00:31:17,600
You’re still the same.

383
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:20,600
No matter how much you two look alike,

384
00:31:22,780 --> 00:31:24,060
I can’t bring myself to like you.

385
00:31:26,070 --> 00:31:27,490
Why did you come back?

386
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:32,650
You are so brazen to come back here.

387
00:31:37,810 --> 00:31:39,960
Sun, you are normally a sweet person.

388
00:31:42,200 --> 00:31:43,860
Why are you so rude to me today?

389
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:46,900
I’m selective about how I treat people.

390
00:31:48,760 --> 00:31:53,400
I’m nice to everyone
except those who f*ck my sister up.

391
00:31:59,180 --> 00:32:00,970
I just came back to get what is mine back.

392
00:32:03,280 --> 00:32:06,400
Do you think
my sister will let you fool her again?

393
00:32:10,030 --> 00:32:12,300
Love is not about being smart or stupid.

394
00:32:13,390 --> 00:32:14,870
It’s about finding a good match.

395
00:32:16,200 --> 00:32:17,800
If we are a good match,

396
00:32:19,290 --> 00:32:21,170
no one can come between us.

397
00:34:34,100 --> 00:34:38,300
♪ Just look into my eyes
a little while longer ♪

398
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:50,080
♪ Every action will make
the memory stronger ♪

399
00:34:51,120 --> 00:34:54,800
♪ Let your feelings slowly grow ♪

400
00:34:55,840 --> 00:35:02,380
♪ And you will remember only me ♪

401
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:08,750
Chan.

402
00:35:09,670 --> 00:35:10,930
Did I wake you up?

403
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:17,400
What is the title of the song?

404
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:24,300
It’s a song that I’m writing.

405
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:27,300
I’ve never performed it for anyone.

406
00:35:28,560 --> 00:35:30,410
You are the first person
to hear this song.

407
00:35:39,850 --> 00:35:40,800
It’s beautiful.

408
00:35:41,750 --> 00:35:42,570
I like it.

409
00:35:44,070 --> 00:35:45,100
Can you sing it again?

410
00:35:48,620 --> 00:35:52,600
Why don’t you sing along with me?

411
00:36:03,750 --> 00:36:09,100
♪ Just look into my eyes
a little while longer ♪

412
00:36:10,250 --> 00:36:14,900
♪ Let your heart get closer to mine ♪

413
00:36:16,790 --> 00:36:23,300
♪ Try to explore what love truly means ♪

414
00:36:24,710 --> 00:36:30,700
♪ One night is not enough for us ♪

415
00:36:33,300 --> 00:36:37,000
♪ I want to love you every day ♪

416
00:36:37,870 --> 00:36:44,900
♪ Close to me, you only one ♪

417
00:36:49,740 --> 00:36:55,700
♪ I’ll make you love and remember me ♪

418
00:36:56,280 --> 00:37:01,200
♪ I’ll keep showing you
until you love me ♪

419
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:09,800
♪ Every touch will remind you of me ♪

420
00:37:10,870 --> 00:37:22,780
♪ Every embrace and every action
will make the memory stronger ♪

421
00:37:23,910 --> 00:37:27,900
♪ Let your feelings slowly grow ♪

422
00:37:28,830 --> 00:37:37,300
♪ And you will remember only me ♪

423
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:49,670
It’s beautiful.

424
00:37:51,820 --> 00:37:53,200
Why don’t you finish the song?

425
00:37:56,680 --> 00:37:57,700
Sure.

426
00:38:01,160 --> 00:38:02,200
But…

427
00:38:04,560 --> 00:38:06,850
Don’t you have something else
you want me to do right now?

428
00:38:07,960 --> 00:38:10,500
You’re a little perv.

429
00:38:23,440 --> 00:38:24,600
Do you like it?

430
00:38:26,980 --> 00:38:27,900
Yes.

431
00:38:56,610 --> 00:38:57,600
From now on,

432
00:39:00,630 --> 00:39:01,920
I have a new rule.

433
00:39:05,170 --> 00:39:06,500
The two of us,

434
00:39:08,860 --> 00:39:10,250
we will not kiss.

435
00:39:17,800 --> 00:39:20,080
We can’t kiss? What do you want me to do?

436
00:39:21,520 --> 00:39:22,700
We won’t kiss.

437
00:39:23,870 --> 00:39:25,000
This is a strict rule.

438
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:26,870
Do you get it?

439
00:39:29,410 --> 00:39:31,100
It will be hard for me.

440
00:39:34,430 --> 00:39:36,100
Why do we need to have this rule?

441
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:47,500
You don’t need to know the reason.

442
00:39:48,850 --> 00:39:50,700
Just do what I told you to do.

443
00:40:00,920 --> 00:40:03,010
Since you won’t let me
kiss you on the lips,

444
00:40:05,620 --> 00:40:07,850
can you kiss my tattoo instead?

445
00:40:50,240 --> 00:40:52,300
♪ You're surely right ♪

446
00:40:53,130 --> 00:40:56,360
♪ You don’t love me
for just one day, right? ♪

447
00:40:56,870 --> 00:40:59,410
♪ Will you stay with me
through days and nights? ♪

448
00:40:59,460 --> 00:41:03,300
♪ Each morning,
will I see your face next to mine? ♪

449
00:41:03,800 --> 00:41:05,980
♪ You’re not just making my heart waver ♪

450
00:41:06,110 --> 00:41:12,500
♪ Then leave me forever, no ♪

451
00:41:26,860 --> 00:41:29,760
Simba, get off me. You’re heavy.

452
00:41:32,650 --> 00:41:34,300
Simba.

453
00:41:53,660 --> 00:41:55,180
We can’t kiss.

454
00:41:56,760 --> 00:41:58,550
So you do this instead.

455
00:42:27,280 --> 00:42:31,730
I want your restaurant
to launch a sale promotion for my hotel.

456
00:42:32,370 --> 00:42:37,370
You will offer 15% off all meal courses
for the hotel guests for one year.

457
00:42:38,910 --> 00:42:41,900
In return, I’ll agree to let you
open your restaurant in my hotel.

458
00:42:42,930 --> 00:42:45,400
And I won’t charge you rent
for the first month.

459
00:42:46,780 --> 00:42:47,800
About that.

460
00:42:48,870 --> 00:42:50,380
I need to ask my partner first.

461
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:53,600
Who is your partner?

462
00:42:56,340 --> 00:42:57,100
Phu.

463
00:42:58,860 --> 00:43:00,200
Who is your partner?

464
00:43:00,350 --> 00:43:01,180
Tell me.

465
00:43:01,840 --> 00:43:02,700
Sun.

466
00:43:03,790 --> 00:43:04,900
Who is helping you?

467
00:43:06,120 --> 00:43:06,900
Sun.

468
00:43:07,700 --> 00:43:08,650
What did you know?

469
00:43:09,470 --> 00:43:11,400
Chan, I…

470
00:43:25,160 --> 00:43:26,000
Hi.

471
00:43:28,420 --> 00:43:29,720
Do you miss me?

472
00:43:46,620 --> 00:43:47,900
Your restaurant.

473
00:43:48,030 --> 00:43:49,300
It’s Jay’s plan, isn’t it?

474
00:43:53,330 --> 00:43:54,330
I’m sorry.

475
00:43:57,710 --> 00:43:59,300
Jay ordered me to do it.

476
00:44:00,740 --> 00:44:02,810
I’m in a tough spot myself.

477
00:44:04,850 --> 00:44:07,720
I know Chan won’t be okay with it.

478
00:44:09,830 --> 00:44:11,290
Is it because you owe Jay money?

479
00:44:15,140 --> 00:44:15,900
Phu.

480
00:44:16,350 --> 00:44:19,830
You end up like this because
you’re living above your means.

481
00:44:21,060 --> 00:44:24,700
I know that you borrowed money
from many people.

482
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:28,520
Even the director I work with,
you also borrowed money from him.

483
00:44:28,910 --> 00:44:30,200
But I never flake on them.

484
00:44:30,920 --> 00:44:32,110
I’m gradually paying them back.

485
00:44:32,150 --> 00:44:33,300
I’m never late on my payment.

486
00:44:33,370 --> 00:44:35,100
But the money that you pay them back,

487
00:44:35,710 --> 00:44:37,050
it’s Jay’s money.

488
00:44:41,980 --> 00:44:43,700
We’ve known each other
for a long time, Phu.

489
00:44:44,360 --> 00:44:45,800
You are Chan’s friend.

490
00:44:46,930 --> 00:44:48,720
If you continue to do this,

491
00:44:49,050 --> 00:44:51,800
I will cut you off one day.

492
00:45:06,980 --> 00:45:08,170
I miss you.

493
00:45:15,320 --> 00:45:16,900
Don’t be mad at Phu.

494
00:45:18,420 --> 00:45:19,900
I forced him to do this.

495
00:45:21,330 --> 00:45:22,870
I told you.

496
00:45:23,450 --> 00:45:25,300
I really want to do business with you.

497
00:45:27,100 --> 00:45:29,320
Don’t let our relationship
be a problem for the business.

498
00:45:30,800 --> 00:45:31,800
I’m asking you.

499
00:45:33,710 --> 00:45:35,800
It won’t affect the restaurant.

500
00:45:37,050 --> 00:45:38,380
It’s a business.

501
00:45:40,270 --> 00:45:41,800
You just do your work.

502
00:45:42,830 --> 00:45:44,300
It has nothing to do with me.

503
00:45:45,800 --> 00:45:47,100
You are the same.

504
00:45:48,950 --> 00:45:51,500
This is my Chan.

505
00:46:16,620 --> 00:46:18,150
Will you have dinner with me tonight?

506
00:46:34,860 --> 00:46:35,800
I knew it.

507
00:46:48,740 --> 00:46:50,200
If you are done with your business,

508
00:46:52,530 --> 00:46:53,530
you should leave.

509
00:46:55,890 --> 00:46:57,200
Before I leave,

510
00:47:00,690 --> 00:47:02,380
can I have a goodbye kiss?

511
00:47:22,950 --> 00:47:27,450
Do you remember I told you this?

512
00:47:29,440 --> 00:47:33,900
Kissing is like smoking.

513
00:47:38,290 --> 00:47:40,240
I quit smoking for a while.

514
00:47:43,610 --> 00:47:45,860
But when I see it again.

515
00:47:50,380 --> 00:47:53,100
I’m more excited
than the first time I smoked.

516
00:48:03,340 --> 00:48:04,700
Do you feel the same as I do?

517
00:48:17,110 --> 00:48:17,900
Fine.

518
00:48:21,080 --> 00:48:22,200
I’m leaving.

519
00:48:26,190 --> 00:48:27,270
See you.

520
00:48:41,980 --> 00:48:43,030
It’s beautiful.

521
00:48:44,130 --> 00:48:45,000
Really?

522
00:48:46,080 --> 00:48:47,200
Do you want to play with me?

523
00:49:52,110 --> 00:49:54,000
Why isn’t she home yet?

524
00:50:07,830 --> 00:50:10,000
Simba, you miss Mama too, right?

525
00:50:54,710 --> 00:50:57,300
Chan smells so good.

526
00:52:28,750 --> 00:52:29,900
Don’t touch my piano.

527
00:52:35,450 --> 00:52:36,550
I’m sorry.

528
00:52:38,530 --> 00:52:41,600
You have no right to touch my stuff
without my permission,

529
00:52:42,190 --> 00:52:43,600
especially this piano.

530
00:52:44,450 --> 00:52:45,410
Do you get it?

531
00:52:48,910 --> 00:52:49,660
Yes.

532
00:52:51,220 --> 00:52:52,250
I get it.

533
00:53:01,250 --> 00:53:02,100
Sorry.

534
00:53:04,780 --> 00:53:07,000
I just don’t like
when people touch my piano.

535
00:53:10,930 --> 00:53:12,300
Can I ask?

536
00:53:16,140 --> 00:53:19,200
What’s the matter with this piano?

537
00:53:25,450 --> 00:53:26,500
This piano,

538
00:53:29,320 --> 00:53:31,070
it belongs to someone who hurt me.

539
00:53:35,440 --> 00:53:36,900
Someone I don’t want to talk about.

540
00:53:54,550 --> 00:53:55,700
I promise.

541
00:53:58,830 --> 00:54:01,050
I will never touch this piano again.

542
00:54:04,710 --> 00:54:06,680
I will also keep Simba away from it.

543
00:54:10,340 --> 00:54:11,800
If it’s Simba,

544
00:54:12,980 --> 00:54:14,100
I don’t mind.

545
00:54:18,130 --> 00:54:19,030
What?

546
00:54:19,800 --> 00:54:21,070
You are playing favorites.

547
00:54:22,660 --> 00:54:23,400
Why?

548
00:54:24,340 --> 00:54:25,680
Do you have a problem with that?

549
00:54:30,150 --> 00:54:31,300
No.

550
00:54:37,950 --> 00:54:40,200
As your sugar baby,

551
00:54:43,620 --> 00:54:45,300
I will never hurt you.

552
00:54:50,030 --> 00:54:51,870
I will never make you feel stressed

553
00:54:54,050 --> 00:54:55,300
or upset.

554
00:54:57,140 --> 00:54:58,770
In the time we spend together,

555
00:55:00,390 --> 00:55:02,000
you will feel only happiness.

556
00:55:04,360 --> 00:55:08,200
From now on, making you smile

557
00:55:10,710 --> 00:55:12,400
It will be my main duty.

558
00:55:22,050 --> 00:55:23,200
Do you feel better?

559
00:55:26,770 --> 00:55:27,580
Yes.

560
00:55:31,040 --> 00:55:32,800
When you smile like this,

561
00:55:34,170 --> 00:55:35,480
I’m in trouble.

562
00:55:36,910 --> 00:55:37,800
Why?

563
00:55:38,200 --> 00:55:40,200
I’m just your sugar baby.

564
00:55:41,900 --> 00:55:43,000
I can’t kiss you.

565
00:55:45,020 --> 00:55:46,650
When I see you smile,

566
00:55:47,530 --> 00:55:48,870
I want to kiss you.

567
00:55:51,950 --> 00:55:53,700
Since you’re my sugar baby,

568
00:55:55,960 --> 00:55:57,340
you can kiss me on the cheek.

569
00:55:58,330 --> 00:55:59,460
I’ll let you do it.

570
00:56:01,650 --> 00:56:02,700
Then I’ll do it.

571
00:56:30,090 --> 00:56:33,100
The kiss on the forehead is a bonus.

572
00:56:49,380 --> 00:56:50,260
Chan.

573
00:56:52,170 --> 00:56:53,400
This girl.

574
00:56:54,270 --> 00:56:55,270
Who is she?

575
00:57:17,990 --> 00:57:19,180
What are you doing here?

576
00:57:19,530 --> 00:57:21,690
I just want to try your hotel service.

577
00:57:22,430 --> 00:57:25,650
I think she wants to get back with you.

578
00:57:26,090 --> 00:57:29,100
What are you thinking,
being her sugar baby?

579
00:57:30,090 --> 00:57:30,850
Bye.

580
00:57:30,910 --> 00:57:32,600
Why are you doing this, Key?

581
00:57:33,360 --> 00:57:35,900
We broke up, Jay. Don’t do this.

582
00:57:36,680 --> 00:57:38,320
But now I’m back.

583
00:57:38,750 --> 00:57:40,570
What if Chan refuses to get back with you?

584
00:57:40,610 --> 00:57:41,850
I want you to move on.

585
00:57:45,170 --> 00:57:48,520
I want you to know that this is my job.

586
00:57:49,390 --> 00:57:51,100
I’ll help you forget her.

587
00:57:51,580 --> 00:57:53,400
You will remember only me.
